# Retrieval evaluation cases. One JSON object per line; the first line is the dataset header.
# Ground truth = owner (user) + document file name + a fragment the relevant chunk contains, so it survives re-chunking.
# "chunkHint" is only a hint for humans (0-based position at the time of writing); a fragment always wins over it.
# "answerable" is explicit on every case. answerable=false means the corpus has no answer (expectedSources must be []):
#   the question must not be sent to the model with weak context. answerable=true needs at least one expected source.
# "split" is fixed by hand, never random: "calibration" cases are used to choose thresholds and ranking variants,
#   "validation" cases are only reported afterwards. Do not move a case between splits after looking at its result.
# semantic-only: the question shares (almost) no word with the answer, so only vector search can find it.
# Tags: paraphrase | semantic-only | exact-term | error-code | file-reference | version | quoted-phrase | short-query | split-info | ambiguous | multi-document | isolation | no-answer
# No-answer kinds: unrelated | missing-fact | similar-terms | wrong-entity | missing-file | missing-identifier | cross-user
{"dataset":{"version":2,"description":"32 original cases + 16 answerable and 13 no-answer cases for confidence calibration; explicit answerable and fixed calibration/validation split."}}
